Build a full-stack personal finance and monthly salary allocation web application using React for the frontend, NestJS for the backend API, and PostgreSQL for the database.

The app should help a user manage monthly salary by splitting it into categories such as:

Wants

Needs

Investments

Loan repayments

Gym

Bike service

Bike petrol

Hostel rent

Other custom expense reasons

Each expense reason should belong to a higher-level category like wants, needs, or investments.

Main goals
User can enter monthly salary/income.

User can allocate planned budget amounts to each expense reason.

User can record actual spending transactions against those reasons.

User can see remaining balance after all allocations/spending.

User can view dashboards to understand where money is going.

User can compare current month vs previous month spending.

User can identify which category has the highest spending priority.

Required features
1. Authentication
Simple login/register for a single user or multi-user support.

JWT-based authentication using NestJS.

2. Monthly budget management
Create monthly budget entries.

Store salary credited for the month.

Add planned allocations under each reason.

Show total allocated, total spent, and remaining balance.

3. Expense tracking
Add, edit, delete expense records.

Each expense should have:

date

amount

reason

category (wants / needs / investments)

notes

month/year

Support recurring monthly expenses like rent, loan, gym, bike service, petrol.

4. Dashboard analytics
Pie chart showing spending percentage by category:

wants

needs

investments

Bar chart for monthly comparison.

Line chart for spending trend over time.

Cards for:

total salary

total spent

total remaining

category-wise spending

top spending reason

5. Comparison and insights
Compare current month vs previous month.

Show whether wants spending increased or decreased.

Show category-wise percentage change.

Highlight overspending against budget.

Show alerts for low remaining balance.

6. Filters and reports
Filter by month, year, category, and reason.

Search transactions.

Export data to Excel or CSV.

View summary reports.

Database design
Create PostgreSQL tables for:

users

monthly_budgets

categories

expense_reasons

transactions

budget_allocations

recurring_expenses

Backend API
Create REST APIs for:

authentication

monthly salary creation

budget allocation management

expense CRUD

dashboard summary

monthly comparison report

chart data endpoints

Frontend pages
Login/Register page

Dashboard page

Add Salary/Budget page

Add Expense page

Monthly Summary page

Reports/Analytics page

Category management page

UI requirements
Clean and modern finance dashboard UI.

Responsive design for desktop and mobile.

Use charts and cards to visualize data clearly.

Use React component-based structure.

Use reusable form components and table components.

Tech stack
Frontend: React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Chart.js or Recharts

Backend: NestJS, TypeScript, Prisma or TypeORM

Database: PostgreSQL

Additional logic
Salary should be divided into multiple planned buckets.

Expenses should reduce the remaining balance automatically.

Dashboard should calculate percentage spent per category.

Previous month comparison should be based on same category totals.